    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- TEST -->
<section id="test" style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <div class="eyebrow">Usability testing</div>
      <h2>Four first-time users, five tasks, think-aloud</h2>
      <p class="lede">Moderated remote sessions over Zoom. Each participant signed up, created two companions, sent text and voice messages, used AR, recorded a mood entry and changed three settings.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="method">
      <div><b>Moderated + think-aloud</b><span>Facilitator, observer and recorded sessions, about 30 minutes each</span></div>
      <div><b>SEQ after every task</b><span>1 = very easy, 7 = very difficult, plus time on task and error counts</span></div>
      <div><b>UMUX-Lite after the test</b><span>We also ran an AI-simulated user pass to cross-check problem areas</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="chart" role="img" aria-label="Average time on task in seconds: Task 1 117, Task 2 83.5, Task 3 145, Task 4 116.5, Task 5 123.5. Average SEQ: 1.25, 1.5, 2.0, 2.25, 1.25.">
      <div class="axis"><span>Task</span><div><span>0s</span><span>75s</span><span>150s</span></div><span style="text-align:right">time · SEQ</span></div>
      <div class="row"><span>1 · Sign up, create 2 companions</span><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:78%"></div></div><span class="v"><b>117s</b> · 1.25</span></div>
      <div class="row"><span>2 · Text and voice message</span><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:55.7%"></div></div><span class="v"><b>84s</b> · 1.50</span></div>
      <div class="row"><span>3 · Enter AR mode</span><div class="track"><div class="fill hot" style="width:96.7%"></div></div><span class="v"><b>145s</b> · 2.00</span></div>
      <div class="row"><span>4 · Record a mood entry</span><div class="track"><div class="fill hot" style="width:77.7%"></div></div><span class="v"><b>117s</b> · 2.25</span></div>
      <div class="row"><span>5 · Text size, theme, voice</span><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:82.3%"></div></div><span class="v"><b>124s</b> · 1.25</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="cap note">Bars show average time on task. Tasks 3 and 4 had the highest difficulty ratings. UMUX-Lite averaged 91.67, with one participant giving 100.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- FINDINGS -->
<section id="findings" style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <div class="eyebrow">Findings and redesign</div>
      <h2>What broke, and what we changed</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="find">
      <div class="t">
        <span class="tag">Finding 1 · emotional timing</span>
        <h3>The AI pushed a feature when the user needed comfort</h3>
        <p>When a participant described a stressful day, the companion offered a tarot reading. Task 2 had four operational errors and the AI tool flagged it as the highest-risk moment.</p>
        <p class="q">“I just poured out my feelings about having a stressful day, and the companion completely ignored my emotional state to suggest a Tarot reading.”</p>
        <p>We removed the automatic pop-up and moved tarot into a “Mystic Tools” entry in the side menu, so users open it when they want to.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ba">
        <figure><span class="k">Before</span><div class="ph"><img src="/media/echo/p-tarot-before.jpg" alt="Before: a pop-up in the chat asks Do you want to open Mystic Tools? with Yes and No buttons"><span class="hl" style="left:6%;top:53%;width:88%;height:24%"></span></div></figure>
        <figure class="after"><span class="k">After</span><div class="ph"><img src="/media/echo/p-sidebar-after.jpg" alt="After: the side menu lists Mood Diary and Mystic Tools as user-initiated entries"><span class="hl" style="left:2%;top:11.5%;width:68%;height:6.5%"></span></div></figure>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="fixes">
      <div class="fix">
        <span class="tag">Finding 2 · findability</span>
        <h3>The mood diary was hard to find and had no clear next step</h3>
        <p>Task 4 had the worst SEQ (2.25). The diary lived only inside Profile, and the calendar looked like a report with no obvious way to add an entry. We added a Mood Diary entry to the side menu and a clear “Add Mood Diary” button on the list and calendar.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="fix">
        <span class="tag">Finding 3 · wording</span>
        <h3>Vague labels and jargon raised the learning curve</h3>
        <p>One participant thought they had to finish the avatar before being logged in. Another did not know what “The Cross” spread meant. We rewrote onboarding copy and added short in-context hints.</p>
        <div class="swap"><s>Create Your Companion</s><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><b>Customize your AI avatar</b></div>
        <div class="swap"><s>The Cross</s><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><b>Select 3 cards</b></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="learned" style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head"><div class="eyebrow">What I took away</div><h2>Designing for feelings</h2></div>
    <div class="learn">
      <div><h3>Timing is part of the interface</h3><p>The same feature can feel helpful or rude depending on when it appears. Emotional state should gate what the product offers.</p></div>
      <div><h3>High scores can hide friction</h3><p>UMUX-Lite was above 90, yet think-aloud showed hesitation in AR and the diary. Watching people matters more than the score.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Less jargon, more guidance</h3><p>Small copy changes, like naming the action instead of the concept, removed confusion that no visual polish could fix.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
